{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>A gracious woman</b> — A possessor of grace and beauty, she supports her honor, that they honor her because of her beauty. Or \"honor\" hints at wealth, and this is the correct interpretation in my eyes. The \"supporting\" is that she does not spend from it for her needs and desires the gifts of others." "<b>And the ruthless</b> — The terrifying ones will support their wealth through the abundance of gifts of others whom they bribe, but."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The comment ends abruptly with אבל (\"but\"), evidently introducing the contrast of the verse's second half; translated hyper-literally as it appears."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:11.028251899Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}